  "query_preview": "../Sunday through Tuesday/... Rain continues across \nthe panhandle as we move out of the weekend and into the week. \nHowever, rain rates appear to be lightening up from moderate and \npersistent to light and showery over the day Sunday. There could \nbe periods of heavier showers on the inner eastern part of the \npanhandle -- Juneau, Petersburg, Wrangell -- through the day \nMonday. Winds across the panhandle continue to diminish through \nthe day Sunday as the low jumps onto land in the western gulf. \nHigh winds from channeling the previous day have the potential to \nlinger in the inner channels across the panhandle with models \npicking up on Stephens Passage in particular. At the same time, \nwinds in Lynn Canal look to increase through the day Sunday and be\nsustained around 20 mph as the pressure gradient over the \npanhandle squeezes.",
